{"id": "EUVD-2026-108683", "enisaUuid": "2969fd4a-2d08-3601-8d9a-9365001e3c93", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mvm: fix sched scan IE sizing\n\nScheduled scan built the probe request before iwl_mvm_scan_fits(),\nso oversized IEs could be copied into the fixed preq buffer before\nlength validation. Move iwl_mvm_build_scan_probe() after the fits\ncheck.\n\nAlso advertise max_sched_scan_ie_len using iwl_mvm_max_scan_ie_len()\nso userspace limits account for driver-inserted DS/TPC bytes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2268060e99f94314b9988dfa17393c2694fa9b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/358eca9a898ad4cce7453e9dcfd005d019a2b01f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05f79cea3b15cfe600b205ddcfd51ebee15d908a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a24417478f90e9f1a4ea24cd4b784afccb56fbae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a63f98e5163a2ec2822dfb691ee5a6094de08ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f155d262b31b9b17e0f9856bdabe0968eb4930f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98889"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00d35f56-500f-34ed-b067-a2c41358f672", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <f2268060e99f94314b9988dfa17393c2694fa9b2"}, {"id": "0374ac8c-0a99-3bdd-b570-f2ac4dd7c610", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "349bdeb5-02d5-3893-9093-fb4103e12e49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "3cca2661-65aa-30af-8b4a-d7be11a4fe7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4f155d262b31b9b17e0f9856bdabe0968eb4930f"}, {"id": "4530ff62-4a62-3fd2-8f0e-d740b99268e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend